<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τλη-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τλᾱτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>patient, steadfast in suffering</i> or
			<i>labour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.49
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be endured</i>, always with neg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ τ</span>. not <i>to be endured</i>,
				in<i>tolerable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γὰρ δή που τοῦτό γε τλητὸν . .
					ἔπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1065
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔστι τοὔγρον
			τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				466
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ τλητόν [ἐστι</span>], c.
				inf., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				797
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alc.</u>
				887
			</span></i> (anap.).</div>
